==============================================================================
  Mutation tests  (assertion-strength validation)
==============================================================================

  Strategy: replace each named fact's body with `{}` (no constraint),
  then re-run Alloy. Each listed assertion should now FAIL on the
  mutated model. If it still PASSes, the assertion is vacuous and
  must be strengthened.

  - MUTATE F_OwnerNotSelfSharee  → runs/B-L3/mutated_F_OwnerNotSelfSharee.als
    rationale: removing this fact lets a Task list its own owner in shared_with; the injection forces such a Task to exist, which NoSelfMutation should catch.
    expected to FAIL: NoSelfMutation
      - NoSelfMutation: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_SharedWithSameTeam  → runs/B-L3/mutated_F_SharedWithSameTeam.als
    rationale: without this fact, sharees can be from a foreign team; the injection forces a cross-team sharee, violating FR-012.
    expected to FAIL: FR_012_NoCrossTeamSharing
      - FR_012_NoCrossTeamSharing: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_NoCrossTeamAccess  → runs/B-L3/mutated_F_NoCrossTeamAccess.als
    rationale: removing this fact lets a successful Action target a task in a different team; the injection makes such an Action exist, violating cross-team isolation.
    expected to FAIL: FR_006_CrossTeamIsolation, NoInformationLeakage
      - FR_006_CrossTeamIsolation: PASS (vacuous?)
      - NoInformationLeakage: PASS (vacuous?)

  - MUTATE F_AuditActorRoleSnapshot  → runs/B-L3/mutated_F_AuditActorRoleSnapshot.als
    rationale: removing this fact lets the audit entry record a role that doesn't match the actor's persisted role (i.e., role taken from request body); the injection forces a misattributed entry.
    expected to FAIL: AttributionCorrectness, FR_002_RoleFromToken, FR_016_AuditFields
      - AttributionCorrectness: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_002_RoleFromToken: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_016_AuditFields: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AuditOriginatesFromAction  → runs/B-L3/mutated_F_AuditOriginatesFromAction.als
    rationale: removing this fact allows an AuditEntry to exist without any producing Action (orphan or fabricated); the injection forces such an orphan, which AppendOnly should reject.
    expected to FAIL: AppendOnly, FR_017_AuditImmutable, FR_020_AuditRetention
      - AppendOnly: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_017_AuditImmutable: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_020_AuditRetention: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AccessMatrix  → runs/B-L3/mutated_F_AccessMatrix.als
    rationale: removing the access-matrix definition lets Alloy populate forbidden cells; the injection forces (TeamAdminRel -> PatchTaskShare) to be allowed, which directly violates the FR-005 / FR-010 invariant that share-list changes are owner-only.
    expected to FAIL: LeastPrivilege, FR_005_AdminCantChangeShare, FR_010_OnlyOwnerChangesShares
      - LeastPrivilege: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_005_AdminCantChangeShare: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_010_OnlyOwnerChangesShares: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AuditCompletenessFact  → runs/B-L3/mutated_F_AuditCompletenessFact.als
    rationale: removing this fact allows a successful mutation Action to produce zero audit entries; the injection forces such an Action to exist, violating per-event audit completeness.
    expected to FAIL: AuditCompleteness, FR_015_AuditPerEvent, ValidationBeforeMutation
      - AuditCompleteness: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_015_AuditPerEvent: FAIL (expected)
      - ValidationBeforeMutation: FAIL (expected)

